{"arrivo":"nl","origine":"ofs","origine_nome":"Old Frisian","livello2":"gmw-pro","livello2_nome":"Proto-West Germanic","n":5,"parole":[{"parola":"eiland","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"no","significato":"island","termine_origine":"eiland","catena":[{"codice":"ofs","nome":"Old Frisian","termine":"eiland","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"gmw-pro","nome":"Proto-West Germanic","termine":"*auwjuland","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"gem-pro","nome":"Proto-Germanic","termine":"*awjōlandą","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"gem-pro","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"From Middle Dutch eilant, from Old Dutch *eilant, from Old Frisian eiland, from Proto-West Germanic *auwjuland, from Proto-Germanic *awjōlandą, equivalent to ei (“island”) + land (“land”). The former part is from *awjō, the latter identical to modern Dutch land."},{"parola":"kaag","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"no","significato":"a tract of land unprotected by any dykes","termine_origine":"kāg","catena":[{"codice":"ofs","nome":"Old Frisian","termine":"kāg","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"gmw-pro","nome":"Proto-West Germanic","termine":"*kaug","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"gmw-pro","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"From Middle Dutch câech, borrowed from Old Frisian kāg, from Proto-West Germanic *kaug."},{"parola":"kies","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"no","significato":"molar","termine_origine":"kēse","catena":[{"codice":"ofs","nome":"Old Frisian","termine":"kēse","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"gmw-pro","nome":"Proto-West Germanic","termine":"*kūsiju","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"gmw-pro","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"From Middle Dutch kiese (late), borrowed from Old Frisian kēse, from Proto-West Germanic *kūsiju. Displaced older kuis, from Middle Dutch *cuse, from the same Proto-West Germanic source."},{"parola":"ladder","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"no","significato":"a ladder","termine_origine":"hladder","catena":[{"codice":"ofs","nome":"Old Frisian","termine":"hladder","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"gmw-pro","nome":"Proto-West Germanic","termine":"*hlaidriju","categoria":"ereditato"},{"codice":"gem-pro","nome":"Proto-Germanic","termine":"*hlaidrijō","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"gem-pro","ambiti":["finanza","moda"],"via":"","testo":"From Middle Dutch ladere, from Old Frisian hladder, hledder, hleder, hlērde, from Proto-West Germanic *hlaidriju, from Proto-Germanic *hlaidrijō."},{"parola":"tillen","pos":"verb","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"sì","motivo_incerta":"Of uncertain origin; Possibly","significato":"to lift, to raise","termine_origine":"","catena":[{"codice":"ofs","nome":"Old Frisian","termine":"","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"gmw-pro","nome":"Proto-West Germanic","termine":"*þolēn","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"gmw-pro","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"From Middle Dutch tillen, of uncertain origin, possibly a borrowing from Old Frisian, and ultimately related to Proto-West Germanic *þolēn (“to endure, bear”)."}]}